# --- Notion: the team section ---------------------------------------------
# The team is read from Notion in a server component and cached for an hour,
# so these are read on the server only and never reach the browser. Without
# them the team section renders its empty state rather than failing the
# build.
#
# The integration also has to be given the database: open it in Notion,
# then ⋯ → Connections → add the integration. Notion answers 404, not 403,
# for a database it cannot see, so a correct id fails exactly like a wrong
# one until you do.
NOTION_SECRET_API_KEY=
NOTION_MEMBER_DATABASE_ID=

# --- Contact form ----------------------------------------------------------
# Web3Forms. Get a key at https://web3forms.com by entering the address the
# mail should arrive at — currently yuchan.7im@gmail.com. The key is emailed
# to that address, and it IS the destination: the API has no recipient
# field, so mail follows the key. To send somewhere else, issue a new key.
#
# Read inside a server action, so it never reaches the browser. Web3Forms
# can be called straight from a page, but then the key ships in the bundle
# and anyone can post through it.
#
# Free tier is 250 submissions a month. Unset, the form says it is not
# connected rather than claiming a message was received.
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
